According to the documented rule for conformance.kernel.recovery, 'The object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one, else the last top-level object in the text' [65ae18af7a738b26]. In the input fence[ A B ] A, the code fence contains JSON objects A and B. Since the fence holds objects, the last one inside (B) is the scored object. In the rewritten text fence[ A ] A, the JSON object B is removed from inside the code fence, leaving only object A inside the fence. Since the fence still holds an object, the last one inside (A) is now the scored object. Thus the recovered object moves from {"b": 2} to {"a": 1}.